---
term: Member
aka:
  - Membership
section: building-blocks
order: 40
definition: A person or corporation that belongs to a corporation and holds the rights and obligations its charter defines.
seeAlso:
  - exit
  - representation-vector
  - ownership
---
Members hold [[constitutional authority]]. They control how the charter evolves, while executives carry it out. Membership rights are distinct from property rights and from delegated public authority.
